 # Registry Specifications
 
-- [ ] **REG-001**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL normalize surrounding whitespace and ASCII letter case before returning a matching record or NotFound.
-- [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
-- [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
-- [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+## Lookup Interface
+
+- [ ] **REG-LOOKUP-001**: When a serial-number lookup is requested, the system SHALL normalize surrounding whitespace and uppercase ASCII letters, then query the active SQLite index and return either `Found(record, snapshotDate)` or `NotFound(snapshotDate)`.
+- [ ] **REG-LOOKUP-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result regardless of whether a record was found.
+- [ ] **REG-LOOKUP-003**: The system SHALL complete any serial-number lookup within 250 milliseconds on target kiosk hardware (4 GB RAM).
+- [ ] **REG-LOOKUP-004**: Serial-number punctuation (hyphens, slashes, etc.) SHALL be preserved during normalization and remain significant for matching.
+
+## Snapshot Import
+
+- [ ] **REG-IMPORT-001**: When a snapshot is imported, the system SHALL verify its cryptographic signature using the bundled public key.
+- [ ] **REG-IMPORT-002**: If a snapshot has an invalid signature, unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import, retain the active snapshot, and report a specific error.
+- [ ] **REG-IMPORT-003**: During import, the system SHALL construct an indexed SQLite database in a temporary location before validating all records.
+- [ ] **REG-IMPORT-004**: When all records are inserted and indexed, the system SHALL atomically activate the new database by updating the active pointer, ensuring the lookup interface never observes partial or invalid state.
+- [ ] **REG-IMPORT-005**: After activation, the snapshot date MUST be retrievable for any subsequent lookup without further file I/O beyond the active database query.
+
+## Data Integrity
+
+- [ ] **REG-DATA-001**: The system SHALL reject any snapshot with duplicate serial numbers (after normalization).
+- [ ] **REG-DATA-002**: The system SHALL preserve the un-normalized serial number in storage for audit trails and certificate display.
+- [ ] **REG-DATA-003**: If a snapshot import fails partway through, the previous active snapshot remains queryable and no corrupted database is exposed to lookups.
